From: 05yuki <ceu.azul.samu@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:44:33 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] [tier 0] deepseek-v4.1: tool namespaces and the reference's
 turn boundary in the chat encoding

Two changes DeepSeek made to the checkpoint's reference
encoding/encoding.py after SGLang's port was written. Tool namespaces
(reference dba1be0a40aa): a tool may carry a namespace; the prompt shows
namespace::name and a parsed call returns the bare name plus a namespace
field on the tool call (absent when there is none). Current-turn
thinking and tool-result image order (reference 314113f8a7da, same as
sgl-project/sglang#44751): without a tools declaration, reasoning is
dropped only before the latest real user request, and tool-result images
keep prompt order.

tools/dsv41-encoding-check.py in the public repo compares the prompts
and parses with the reference byte for byte.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
